From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rumisle <why-excuse-quail@duck.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:11:58 +0800
Subject: server: /api/session/active reports when each run started; the
 working timer uses it

A page opened or reloaded mid-run used to start the composer's working timer at
the last user message, so a run with a steer or a delivered follow-up looked
like it restarted. The execution service records when each execution started,
/api/session/active returns it as time.started (optional, additive), and the
client data layer seeds runStarted from it on (re)connect; a start event seen
during hydration still wins.

Ocelot-Patch: web/working-timer-resync

